# data-models-relationships

Core business domain entities:

1. Bond Compliance Records
- Tracks check-in history and verification status
- Links between inmates, cases and verification attempts
- Stores geolocation data and timestamps for compliance events
- Associates compliance photos with verification sessions

2. Inmate Management
- Tracks inmate status, bond details and case assignments
- Links to bond compliance verification records
- Associates with agent contact records and notification preferences
- Maintains audit trail of status changes

3. Location Verification
- Caches verified location results with TTL
- Links geographic coordinates to compliance sessions
- Associates VPN/proxy detection results
- Maps boundaries for allowed check-in areas

4. Communication Records
- Stores multi-channel notification statuses (SMS, WhatsApp)
- Links messages to compliance events
- Tracks message delivery attempts and fallbacks
- Associates templates with notification types

Key Relationships:
- Inmates -> Cases (1:M)
- Cases -> Bond Records (1:1)  
- Bond Records -> Compliance Events (1:M)
- Compliance Events -> Location Verifications (1:1)
- Agents -> Cases (M:M)
- Notifications -> Compliance Events (M:1)

Importance Score: 90/100
- Critical domain entities for bond compliance
- Complex relationships between verification components
- Core audit trail requirements
- Mission-critical tracking of inmates and cases

